Subject: Gives callees with captured parameters their own argument copies

What this does
  Gives callees with captured parameters their own argument copies.

Why we need it
  `JS_CallInternal` used the caller's `argv` as the argument area whenever enough arguments were passed; under DRC that is often a register window whose slots do not own their values, and a callee reaching a parameter through a var_ref (closure capture, mapped `arguments`.

What it adds
  Under `QJS_REGVM && QJS_DRC`, a callee with `args_captured` gets owned copies, the same rule `regvm_args_borrowable` already applies on the record path.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -32483,8 +32483,15 @@ static JSValue JS_CallInternal(JSContext *caller_ctx, JSValueConst func_obj,
             return JS_EXCEPTION;
     }
 
+    /* Under DRC the caller's argv may be borrowed registers. A var_ref onto a
+       parameter slot frees the old value on write, so such a callee must own
+       copies, as in regvm_args_borrowable. */
     if (unlikely(argc < b->arg_count ||
-                 ((flags & JS_CALL_FLAG_COPY_ARGV) && !JS_ARGV_SAFE(b)))) {
+                 ((flags & JS_CALL_FLAG_COPY_ARGV) && !JS_ARGV_SAFE(b))
+#if QJS_REGVM && QJS_DRC
+                 || b->args_captured
+#endif
+                 )) {
         arg_allocated_size = b->arg_count;
     } else {
         arg_allocated_size = 0;
